# Backend-only examples. Replace ALL zero IDs with IDs from your own records.
# Tokens must come from normal login for the corresponding active accounts.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7174
@facultyToken = REPLACE_WITH_FACULTY_TOKEN
@hodToken = REPLACE_WITH_ASSIGNED_HOD_TOKEN
@examId = 0
@markId = 0
@approvalId = 0
@versionNo = 0

### Faculty: list existing entries and obtain markId (the entry must belong to this faculty)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks?examId={{examId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{facultyToken}}

### Faculty: submit DRAFT / REJECTED marks. All MarkIds succeed together or nothing changes.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/workflow/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{facultyToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: marks-task13-submit

{
  "examId": {{examId}},
  "markIds": [{{markId}}],
  "sectionId": null,
  "subjectId": null,
  "remarks": "Marks entered and checked."
}

### Assigned HOD: get review queue with approvalId, markId, versionNo and marks
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/approvals/pending?examId={{examId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hodToken}}

### Assigned HOD: spreadsheet route. Copy approvalId and versionNo from the queue.
# {id} is approvalId. ExpectedVersion is optional, but recommended to detect stale review data.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/approvals/{{approvalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hodToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: marks-task13-approve

{
  "status": "APPROVED",
  "remarks": "Verified against the assessment record.",
  "expectedVersion": {{versionNo}}
}

### Alternative HOD decision for a different SUBMITTED entry
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/approvals/{{approvalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hodToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "REJECTED",
  "remarks": "Correct the total and resubmit.",
  "expectedVersion": {{versionNo}}
}

### Existing batch approval route remains available
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/workflow/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{hodToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "examId": {{examId}},
  "markIds": [{{markId}}],
  "remarks": "Verified."
}

### Existing batch rejection route remains available; remarks are required
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/workflow/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{hodToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "examId": {{examId}},
  "markIds": [{{markId}}],
  "remarks": "Correct the total and resubmit."
}

### Faculty: correct a REJECTED entry (SUBMITTED / APPROVED entries are locked)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/{{markId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{facultyToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "marksObtained": 85,
  "maxMarks": 100,
  "remarks": "Total corrected."
}

### Faculty: review own submission / rejection history, then run submit again
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/{{markId}}/approval-history
Authorization: Bearer {{facultyToken}}

### Negative test: empty batch should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/workflow/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{facultyToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "examId": {{examId}},
  "markIds": []
}

### Negative test: faculty approval should return 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/marks/workflow/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{facultyToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "examId": {{examId}},
  "markIds": [{{markId}}]
}
